# The test save mvp-lever (#210, made by `approach lever_0012` in make-test-saves.ps1): a sword in the hand and the
# right hand's reticle on lever_0012 from where the save stands - in the engine's reach, nothing of the level before it;
# then the save loaded again through the channel with the sword held (the regression check of the load crash, #210).
#   .\scripts\dev\smoke-test.ps1 -VrSim idle -Sequence reach-lever -Save mvp-lever
@sim idle
@save mvp-lever
@args --loadslot 0

@until state eq GAMEPLAY 60s
@until vr.sim.timelineFrame ge 270 60s       # 3 s into the level: past its fade-in (TRAPS.md)
@assert player.controlsBlocked eq false
@assert vr.weapon.place eq hand
@until vr.reticle.on eq true 5s

vr-point right entity lever_0012
@frames 10
@assert vr.reticle.right.under eq lever_0012
@assert vr.reticle.right.entity eq lever_0012
@assert ui.hover eq lever_0012
@shot lever

# A load with the sword in the IK hand (#210): the load frees the entities before the hand is updated again, and the
# held weapon's status read the freed sword (a crash at VRWeapon.cpp:296, the radial menu's quick load too)
@mark
loadslot 0
@log level\.loaded 30s
@until state eq GAMEPLAY 60s
@frames 30
@assert vr.weapon.place eq hand
@assert vr.weapon.item eq short_sword_0030
@assert vr.weapon.inHand eq true
@assert errors eq 0
